                          Python 2.7 Quick Reference
                         (AmigaPython 2.7.18 edition)

NOTE: The previous file in this location was Ken Manheimer's 1994
"Python Bestiary".  For AmigaPython 2.7.18 use the official reference:

  https://docs.python.org/2.7/

Amiga-specific behaviour is documented in docs/amiga/ (and
Source/Amiga_Misc/Docs/).  A longer quick-ref also exists upstream as
Source/Misc/cheatsheet (Python 2.3-era; useful but not complete for 2.7).


Invocation (Amiga)
------------------

  Python [options] [script | -c cmd | -] [args...]

Common options: -i -v -S -O -c cmd  (also -? for help on this port)

Environment (ENV: / shell): PYTHONPATH  PYTHONHOME  PYTHONCASEOK
  PYTHONSTARTUP  TMPDIR


Amiga essentials
----------------

  sys.platform == 'amiga'
  import os                 # portable; uses builtin amiga underneath
  import amiga              # Dos / ASL / catalog / icon / crc32 / paths
  os.path                   # Amiga path rules (: absolute, // parent)

  amiga.to_unix / from_unix
  amiga.FileRequest / MessageBox
  amiga.OpenCatalog / DiskObject
  ARexx via arexx / _arexx   (see docs/amiga/arexx_module)


